\f5\b Budget Tracker
\f4\b0 . Users can add and remove income or expense transactions, which are stored as one JSON file per day, and generate reports for a date range with LINQ, all from a simple terminal menu. The project brings together what you have learned about C#: file I/O, JSON serialisation, enums and records, events and error handling. Each requirement below lists the lessons that cover it, and some of them may not be covered yet, so start with the parts you already know and add the rest as you learn them.\cb1 \
