\f4\fs32 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 . See Projections.\cb1 \

\f5\b \cb3 The 
\f4\b0\fs24 \cf8 \cb9 \strokec8 TransactionService
\f5\b\fs32 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4  does not touch files.
\f4\b0  It creates the 
\f7\fs24 \cf8 \cb9 \strokec8 Transaction
\f4\fs32 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4  (Id, Timestamp), asks 
\f7\fs24 \cf8 \cb9 \strokec8 StorageService
\f4\fs32 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4  to save it and then raises the event. Keeping file access in one class makes the next stretch goal much easier.\cb1 \
